{"title":"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4:_Quadratic_Formula\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4: Quadratic Formula</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(with_Simon&#39;s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (with Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:00)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:00)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The zeroes of the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0f0226401b5eb8fafb7cbaed175fcbd0a7a7728.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^2-ax+2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"21\" /> are integers. What is the sum of the possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad274005e946261334794d8f86f18afe302d69f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/57622f0979b9576131025c1f364d7b564bd0e77e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 8\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 16\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 17\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By Vieta's Formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the sum of the integral zeros of the function, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is integral.\n</p><p>Because the zeros are integral, the discriminant of the function, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d2918f3b554aa900474257ddd8ca4e12512adf3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - 8a$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />, is a perfect square, say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/5/0e5c83cc0c639fc2ed843bbe2d3d209fb478b104.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" />. Then adding 16 to both sides and completing the square yields\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/0/0f0fc54cac5d6efbe535f2c0592f14c11a50bde5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a - 4)^2 = k^2 + 16.\\]\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/5/eb52dc1ab5b31bd0be858299953a121c87631dc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-4)^2 - k^2 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"19\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/3/8035bbf221fd1d0b33f061a4dea96f3e9d32f20d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[((a-4) - k)((a-4) + k) = 16.\\]\" width=\"247\" height=\"18\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/8/ae87759823804a2d852416e2599be4763f0189b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-4) - k = u$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/4/77429f40c6a70a7c437b557e0bf992b13ff47944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-4) + k = v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"18\" />; then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659c24bb306049854da5e6c4e2a798e54e5e6086.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a-4 = \\dfrac{u+v}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"109\" height=\"35\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/025b538dba348020cff7b03bc92ea8981bdbc019.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\dfrac{u+v}{2} + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"111\" height=\"35\" />. Listing all possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/1/e4162d79742879fcd196374e6e48a3f896087872.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u, v)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> pairs (not counting transpositions because this does not affect (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/7/387885f0e6ec1245f344fd1b192210e4a689e7f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$u + v$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />)), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d819cecbd136814e8e32ea0045847bbb7e18c441.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 8), (4, 4), (-2, -8), (-4, -4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"240\" height=\"18\" />, yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/a/5da24791113f6c68c3628a4f91dd894cfc2f9fd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 9, 8, -1, 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"108\" height=\"16\" />. These <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> sum to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/b/0db5946ec5998020933dc9ef4064e53212c6ff16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> be the integer zeroes of the quadratic. \nBy <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vieta%27s_Formulas\" title=\"Vieta&#39;s Formulas\">Vieta's Formulas</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241dc901e5926dcdf5ebe9088377efdd9d039a41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_1 + r_2 = a\\text{ and }r_1r_2 = 2a.\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Plugging the first equation in the second, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9944895d19b5830154a28bc2d0135db44595a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_1r_2 = 2 (r_1 + r_2).\\]\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" /> \n</p><p>Rearranging gives \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/d/1dd9b233057fedffe4679c96548d1456eea50935.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[r_1r_2 - 2r_1 - 2r_2 = 0 \\implies (r_1 - 2)(r_2 - 2) = 4.\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>These factors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/d/bed240503706194e2cc2c9f0d6f862900a71f563.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f_1,f_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" /> (ignoring order, because we want the sum of factors), can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac8f449f280743ab44aff517cff4371371f4eca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 4), (-1, -4), (2, 2),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/f/4dfc8ed4ef6b2f3ec098e1f25ded824009c3db4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-2, -2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>The sum of distinct <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/2609a16ff07858180114c157125da71a9c6b3b08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = r_1 + r_2 = (f_1+2) + (f_2+2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"259\" height=\"20\" />, and these factors give \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/9/2b9905af688f723f4eda9ece62a68848593db943.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_a a = (5+4) + (-5+4) + (4+4) + (-4+4) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }16}\\]\" width=\"464\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the roots be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. By Vieta's we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab9c14d43a22ee18cbbdca1f7630e82aa73d7d1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/4/ee417483fc5d398ce8d9f1c6aaa91668f567436b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs = 2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />. So by Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/2/3b2f4e10017f397c7de9c051683b5f3603f901c9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2r+2s = rs \\Longrightarrow rs-2r-2s = 0 \\Longrightarrow (r-2)(s-2) = 4.\\]\" width=\"452\" height=\"18\" /> Now, we test out values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> to see which work. Lets say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbbbd44652c9691b6da5b0503f2e1bd27b6a6f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/6/e3607db4a1439026680761649fc9563ce4bd61cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />. This implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/0/140db35b4b38fafdbc8927a5a810b78f48a0450a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s) = (3,6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac1354558266508b4407741ff1129cb2ab838a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b518f3219cff934c95c4eb694ec8bcc6c6c723ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841de552475f6aec38f5690bc41049ba4362e7d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-2 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"15\" />, this gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/3/1b331fc4dee0c0aa92cc8603fbd280793b355b57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s) = (4,4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, which gives us a value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Now, we circle an answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and move onto the next problem. Yikes! They didn't say that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can't be negative! This is where many people would go wrong. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d57097ae896fe4cf28dbc6afa1b0a7197b8586c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-2 = -1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/a/7fa7bebe72558120b0d13716031e3fbae02aa39a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-2 = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />. This gives us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/f/e5f8c688fc9cf7aa843ab51ca3d5cb1fc67fe1ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r,s) = (1,-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" />. This results in a value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Now, we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2e8a464b43b1dccc6fc3f78fd364552eb48393d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r-2 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/f/c2f04f24bfddca2735b3f5281f00085d84f2d2c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s-2 = -2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />. This gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Now, we are done. Our total sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0a9381fe2e20220e7ebf8c597445995f884d90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+8-1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"162\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-jb2015007 - minor edits by mathlover1205 and PojoDotCom\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4:_Quadratic_Formula\">Solution 4: Quadratic Formula</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4: Quadratic Formula\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are given that the zeroes are integers. For this reason, we should use the quadratic formula on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/7/6d724e3e9b71a7da2b9b9ddd2630915f707de898.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 - ax + 2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" /> to yield more information about the roots. \n</p><p>After simplifying, we get that the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/122f5d5194a207b0dfcc264377b24c6504895b1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{a \\pm \\sqrt{a^2 - 8a}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"43\" />. From this, we can see that a^2 - 8a has to be a perfect square for the roots to be integers. \n</p><p>In addition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/9/d2918f3b554aa900474257ddd8ca4e12512adf3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - 8a$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> have to have the same parity (both even or both odd). However, that is always true (you can try out some odd/even integers)\n</p><p>Hence, I set up another equation: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4dbce818847d076bbab8fb25dab11b6253dde54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 - 8a = y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"101\" height=\"20\" />, where y is an integer.\n</p><p>I use the quadratic formula again for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, yielding that the roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/7/577b26727f5a70e6465762e6174089770b17c0f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\pm \\sqrt{y^2 + 16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"24\" />. If we sum up 2 conjugate roots, the sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the problem boils down to finding nonnegative \"Pythagorean Triples\" with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Hence, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/8/6389a3877e2c9d09826aa0c5e5aa564d8c355afa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/0/7a06334068417b1781d14e8b28af827907961eb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" />. Each contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to the running sum, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/2/232baead1207f7962d526e6375fe2f0828d3fbc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8 + 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Note: We can see that there are at max 2 values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, as the answer choices indicate either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a5b4928c8fe50ce3c2428da3bee3505e891b788.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nP.S. Thanks for the latex formatting. ~DARSHSHETTY4\n</p><p>~DARSHSHETTY4(original solution)\n~biegetomcat72(LaTeX)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28with_Simon.27s_Favorite_Factoring_Trick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(with_Simon's_Favorite_Factoring_Trick)\">Solution 5 (with Simon's Favorite Factoring Trick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (with Simon&#39;s Favorite Factoring Trick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the roots be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>By Vieta, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/9/d497b87e3f1da9053ccff7ff550d6b4440f24413.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r+s=a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8c1a209e2265c9a4187fb6ab39f7eb06482cbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$rs=2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>When we multiply the first equation by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, both equations are equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, so we can set them equal to each other.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/5/22558d977ed01fdab7d0451acd6cec482415fa88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r+2s=rs$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> \n</p><p>Subtracting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e90bed335fface5b59b01fd940ec09c16bb6d0eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r+2s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" /> from both sides, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dd8e4aa042ad0d6c4079cb8e7099ea7998be8bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0=rs-2r-2s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"132\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We add 4 to both sides so that we can apply SFFT.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9abc2c6843a0464bf1463cab1ec346079afbe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=rs-2r-2s+4=(r-2)(s-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"296\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Since the roots are integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/2/4720e3c9d8b934a4683506dac6e66d2247c8cdd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/f/8ffa1f862add8fbcf4fb3b737fc1bd462f8bab9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(s-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> are also integers. \n</p><p>The unordered pairs for {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b1bd7f08490e03fc6f8e365c19043a809fb6da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r-2),(s-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />} that satisfy the above equation are:\n{1,4},\n{2,2},\n{-1,-4},\n{-2,-2}.\nTherefore, the unordered pairs for {<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/4/ba43a2427cd2b08e68760b577866e113c17c7966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r,s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"11\" />} are:\n{3,6},\n{4,4},\n{1,-2},\n{0,0}.\n</p><p><br />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e1abc101b4b54058996ccfd59174421bfb322b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=r+s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"75\" height=\"14\" />, the distinct values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for each pair of roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e93e446d7160b781bc8d59724de8bb62eb6d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1, 0, 8,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/a/f6a1b9d5cec741422bfb37f91db47fd7514f5377.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\nTheir sum is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/149c1d7285022d1c6fb926cbbf1de586304a3c85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"30\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>~mehta0edu\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:00.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:00)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:00)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:00)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/NGBxsSXLGJ4\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/NGBxsSXLGJ4</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p><p>Note: the problem where this is linked is covered 2:00-3:00\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RQ4ZCttwmA4\">https://youtu.be/RQ4ZCttwmA4</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2015amc10a/397\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2015amc10a/397</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A\">2015 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2015 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017010944\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.058 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.079 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 582/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 16706/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.900      1 -total\n 63.83%    8.872      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 35.23%    4.897      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13932:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017010944 and revision id 292286. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}